sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-15> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-15--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-15--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-15: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.48" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.48"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.52"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Counts of repeated parts and their distribution on a tree are measurable, but the progenitor story needs a fossil or ancestral reconstruction that is only partly available. Existing fossil occurrences and matrices can test a subset of vertebrates and arthropods and are weak for the floral-leaf comparison. Circular definitions of 'low' and the co-option alternative keep discriminating power modest." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Test two linked predictions: earlier or less modified members of vertebrates, arthropods and flowering plants show more numerous repeated parts, and ancestral-state or fossil reconstructions give those progenitors many similar segments, vertebrae or leaf-like organs. The claim is confirmed if repetition declines along derived branches and stem fossils are highly repetitive, and refuted if repetition is unrelated to phylogenetic grade or stem fossils already show specialized, non-repeated organs." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "'Low or little-modified' has often been defined by the presence of many repeated parts, which builds the predicted pattern into the ranking.", "A shared patterning pathway can be co-opted later, producing serial organs without an ancestor that already possessed many of them.", "The relevant early fossils are incomplete, especially for soft segmentation and for the origin of floral organs." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-15--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-15--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-15--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-15--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-15 by Grok 4.7: 0.5" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
